{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1043027-appropriate-skills-and-merits-for-ww2-commandos-ala-inglorious-basterds","id":1043027,"title":"Appropriate skills and merits for WW2 commandos, ala Inglorious Basterds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-03T10:36:39-08:00","id":1043027,"title":"Appropriate skills and merits for WW2 commandos, ala Inglorious Basterds","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I'm gearing up to run an Inglorious Basterds/Dirty Dozen game in the World of Darkness, and I want to give the PCs some free skills and merits to represent commando training. Not a lifetime of soldiering, but several months of intense training and education by the OSS. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">What should I do to represent that? My current thought is a free dot in each of the killing skills (Brawl, Firearms, Weaponry) plus 8-10 experience to spend on other commando-type skills and merits. Is that too vague though? Should I just give a flat package of skills and merits? </span></span><i>Which</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> skills and merits? Is there a specific Fighting Style that would be appropriate to WW2-era special forces?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9459-smilingbandit2","name":"smilingbandit2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:47:40-08:00","id":1043068,"title":"","content":"How about 1 free dot in each combat skill and 